<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  gThumb keyboard shortcuts, installed by bootstrap.sh to
  ~/.config/gthumb/shortcuts.xml (plain copy, not stowed: gThumb rewrites the
  file with a full dump of all shortcuts whenever they are edited in its GUI,
  which would spray noise into the repo through a symlink).

  Why: out of the box the viewer binds next/previous FILE to Page_Down/Page_Up
  and uses the bare arrow keys to scroll (pan) the current image. Panning is
  useless at fit-to-window zoom, and arrow-key flipping through a mixed
  image/video folder is the whole point of using gThumb as the viewer. So the
  arrows become next/previous file, and step-scrolling moves to Ctrl+Shift+
  arrows (chosen to dodge the media viewer's seek bindings, which occupy
  Shift/Alt/Ctrl+arrows for 5s/10s/1min skips).

  Bare Right/Left are free in the video viewer too - it only binds MODIFIED
  arrows for seeking - so one flips straight through videos as well; seeking
  within a video still works with Shift/Alt/Ctrl+arrows.

  Format: action names come from the *-actions-entries.h tables in gThumb's
  source; only actions listed here are overridden, everything else keeps its
  default. gThumb's GMarkup-based parser ignores XML comments.
-->
<shortcuts>
  <shortcut action="show-next-image" accelerator="Right"/>
  <shortcut action="show-previous-image" accelerator="Left"/>
  <shortcut action="scroll-step-right" accelerator="&lt;Primary&gt;&lt;Shift&gt;Right"/>
  <shortcut action="scroll-step-left" accelerator="&lt;Primary&gt;&lt;Shift&gt;Left"/>
</shortcuts>
